{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2239","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2239","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2239\",\"parent_revision\":\"2a6e05ad36ae418d5187516319635f359e008e4dd598606887f495899aad218b\",\"root_revision\":\"2a6e05ad36ae418d5187516319635f359e008e4dd598606887f495899aad218b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **per-task subagentstop transcript jsonl persistence in dh state for post-hoc audit** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md \u2014 pattern: Transcript Persistence (`.octogent/projects/&lt;project-id&gt;/state/transcripts/*.jsonl`)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:48015f579a4440d5defac46feca9ce60 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`task_status_hook.py` SubagentStop handler additionally writes (or hard-links) the agent's transcript JSONL to `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/transcripts/{plan-id}/{task-id}-{session-id}.jsonl` after extracting the existing fields. The transcript is written once on SubagentStop. A new MCP tool `task_transcript_read(plan, task, session_id=None)` exposes the path or content for query, complementing the existing `artifact_read` pattern.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source Pattern\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nOctogent (research entry ./research/agent-frameworks/octogent.md): \\\"Transcript Persistence: captures agent conversations to `.octogent/projects/&lt;project-id&gt;/state/transcripts/*.jsonl`\\\". The local equivalent leverages the existing SubagentStop hook that already reads the JSONL but discards the bulk of the content.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun an agent against a SAM task; on SubagentStop, the file `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/transcripts/{plan-id}/{task-id}-{session-id}.jsonl` exists and contains the same content as the original transcript at `~/.claude/projects/...`. `mcp__plugin_dh_sam__task_transcript_read(plan=\\\"P1\\\", task=\\\"T1\\\")` returns a path or content, not an error. A test fixture confirms idempotent re-runs do not duplicate the transcript file.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py` lines 654-720 already include `_extract_prompt_from_transcript` and `_extract_session_id_from_transcript` functions that READ the SubagentStop transcript JSONL to extract specific fields (initial prompt, session_id). The hook does NOT copy or persist a snapshot of the transcript to the DH state directory. Transcripts live only at the Claude Code default path (`~/.claude/projects/...`) and are not aggregated under `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/state/transcripts/` keyed by SAM task ID.\\n\\nWhen investigating \\\"what did agent X do during task T\\\", the only path is to crawl the raw `~/.claude/projects/...` JSONLs, which are not indexed by task ID. This is especially painful for worktree-isolated agents whose transcripts are spread across multiple session directories with no task-aware index.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5155318cc3f50642eeaa9ff012a2068e096210114c0e0408fdda9dbd6fc882a8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSdrcVQ\"}"}